-- Fixture rows that give the system console realistic data to render in a demonstration stack:
-- applications, projects, members, and pending invites for the test-org organization, plus
-- worker nodes and workloads in every state for the orchestrator views. Applied with the `fixtures` profile
-- alone: the e2e suites assert against exact test-org contents and must not see these rows.

-- Applications owned by test-org

-- Projects across the applications above; repoConnectionStatus varies so each state renders

-- Organization members (no credentials — fixture identities never log in): users of test-org, one disabled so the
-- Members table renders the Disabled status

-- Org-level pending invites (no applicationId), each to a pending member an administrator added. Far-future
-- expiresAt keeps them visible: the pending-invite queries filter out expired rows

-- Worker nodes, as a registered node that heartbeats stands: taking workloads, and reconciled on
-- that. The free figures are the totals less the sum of the non-stopped workloads placed on each
-- node below, so capacity bars agree with the workload table. dev-worker-3 reports a problem, so
-- it drains.
-- lastSeen carries milliseconds, the form the server writes: the heartbeat watcher marks a silent
-- node unreachable with a write conditional on lastSeen matching as stored, which a second-precision
-- value never does, leaving a fixture node ONLINE and eligible for placement

-- Workloads covering every WorkloadStatus, both test-org and system (no organizationId)
-- scope, and a PENDING row with no nodeId (not yet placed)
